Create `run-backup.ps1`:

```powershell
# run-backup.ps1
Set-Location -Path "C:\path\to\able-gpt"
npm run backup-config

# Archive logs older than 7 days
$logsDir = "C:\path\to\able-gpt\logs"
$archiveDir = "C:\path\to\able-gpt\logs\archive"

if (-not (Test-Path $archiveDir)) {
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $archiveDir
}

$cutoffDate = (Get-Date).AddDays(-7)

Get-ChildItem -Path $logsDir -File | Where-Object {
    $_.LastWriteTime -lt $cutoffDate -and $_.Name -ne "archive"
} | ForEach-Object {
    $archivePath = Join-Path $archiveDir $_.Name
    Move-Item $_.FullName $archivePath
    Write-Host "Archived log file: $($_.Name)"
}
```

Run to set up the scheduled task:

```cmd
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File schedule-backups.ps1
```

## 8. Troubleshooting

### 8.1 Common Issues and Solutions

| Issue | Potential Cause | Solution |
|-------|-----------------|----------|
| Server won't start | Port already in use | Change the port in .env or stop the process using the port |
| Environment validation fails | Missing or incorrect environment variables | Check .env file against the required variables list |
| Notion API errors | Invalid token or permissions | Verify your integration is properly connected to the workspace |
| GitHub API errors | Rate limiting or invalid token | Check rate limits with a GET to /rate_limit endpoint |
