## Performance Considerations

When scaling to multiple personalities, consider these performance factors:

1. **Memory Usage**:
   - Each personality maintains its own memory collections
   - Use lazy loading to only initialize personalities when needed
   - Consider shared memory for common knowledge

2. **Startup Time**:
   - Implement progressive loading of personalities
   - Initialize only the most commonly used personalities at startup
   - Allow background initialization of others

3. **Response Time**:
   - Cache preprocessed prompts for common queries
   - Optimize memory retrieval with efficient vector indexing
   - Consider parallel processing of memory retrieval and prompt enhancement

4. **Resource Sharing**:
   - Use a shared LLM service to avoid redundant model instances
   - Pool connections to external services like Notion and GitHub
   - Implement rate limiting per personality to prevent resource contention

5. **Scaling Strategy**:
   - Start with a small number of personalities and monitor performance
   - Add personalities incrementally and measure impact
   - Consider API gateway patterns for routing requests to appropriate personalities

# Onboarding Guide for New GPT Personalities

## Table of Contents
1. [Integration with Existing Architecture](#integration-with-existing-architecture)
2. [Onboarding Workflow](#onboarding-workflow)
3. [How Components Work Together](#how-components-work-together)
4. [Integration with AbleGPT and RenascendGPT](#integration-with-ablegpt-and-renascendgpt)
5. [Quick Start Guide](#quick-start-guide)

## Integration with Existing Architecture

The personality extension system is designed to integrate seamlessly with your existing server architecture. Here's how the components fit into the overall system:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      Server Architecture                         │
├────────────────┬──────────────────────┬────────────────────────┐
│                │                      │                        │
│  Next.js API   │    Express Server    │     React Frontend     │
│    Routes      │                      │                        │
│                │                      │                        │
├────────────────┼──────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤
│                │                      │                        │
│ Personality    │  Notion/GitHub       │   Personality         │
│ Service        │  Integration         │   UI Components       │
│                │                      │                        │
├────────────────┼──────────────────────┼────────────────────────┤
│                │                      │                        │
│ ChromaDB       │  LLM Service         │   Memory Manager      │
│ Collections    │  (OpenAI/Claude)     │                        │
│                │                      │                        │
└────────────────┴──────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘
```

Key integration points:

1. **API Routes**: Each personality exposes its endpoints under `/api/personalities/[personality-id]/[endpoint]`
2. **Memory System**: Personalities use ChromaDB collections prefixed with their ID
3. **External APIs**: Access to Notion and GitHub is managed through existing services
4. **UI Components**: Each personality registers its UI components with the frontend

## Onboarding Workflow

Follow this step-by-step workflow to implement and integrate a new personality:

### 1. Define Personality Requirements

Start by clearly defining what your new personality should do:

- **Purpose**: What specialized task or domain will this personality handle?
- **Tone & Style**: How should the personality communicate (formal, casual, technical)?
- **Memory Needs**: What types of information should the personality remember?
- **API Integrations**: Which external APIs does the personality need to access?
- **UI Requirements**: What custom UI elements are needed for this personality?

### 2. Create the Personality Structure

Create a new directory for your personality:

```bash
mkdir -p src/personalities/your-personality-id
```

Inside this directory, create the following files:

```
src/personalities/your-personality-id/
├── index.ts                   # Registration and exports
├── your-personality-id.personality.ts  # Main implementation
├── types.ts                   # Personality-specific types
├── prompts.ts                 # System and user prompts
└── ui/                        # UI components (optional)
    ├── index.ts               # UI exports
    ├── PersonalitySelector.tsx # UI for selecting this personality
    └── CustomComponents.tsx   # Any custom UI components
```

### 3. Implement the Personality Interface

Create your personality class by implementing the `Personality` interface:

```typescript
// src/personalities/your-personality-id/your-personality-id.personality.ts

import { Personality, PersonalityConfig } from '../../types/personality';
import { PersonalityMemoryManager } from '../../services/personalityMemoryService';
import { prompts } from './prompts';

export default class YourPersonality implements Personality {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  description: string;
  version: string;
  systemPrompt: string;
  defaultTemperature: number;
  maxTokens: number;

  private memoryManager: PersonalityMemoryManager;

  constructor(config: PersonalityConfig) {
    this.id = config.id;
    this.name = config.name;
    this.description = config.description;
    this.version = config.version;
    this.systemPrompt = config.systemPrompt;
    this.defaultTemperature = config.defaultTemperature;
    this.maxTokens = config.maxTokens;

    this.memoryManager = new PersonalityMemoryManager(this);
  }

  async initialize(): Promise<void> {
    await this.memoryManager.initialize();
    // Add any additional initialization logic here
  }

  async preparePrompt(input: string, context?: any): Promise<string> {
    // Implement your prompt preparation logic
    return input;
  }

  async processResponse(response: string): Promise<string> {
    // Implement your response processing logic
    return response;
  }

  getMemoryKey(input: string): string {
    return `${this.id}_${input.slice(0, 20).replace(/\W+/g, '_').toLowerCase()}`;
  }

  async shutdown(): Promise<void> {
    // Clean up resources
  }
}
```

### 4. Create Registration File

Register your personality with the system:

```typescript
// src/personalities/your-personality-id/index.ts

import { registerNewPersonality } from '../../services/personalityService';
import YourPersonality from './your-personality-id.personality';
import { prompts } from './prompts';

registerNewPersonality({
  id: 'your-personality-id',
  name: 'Your Personality Name',
  description: 'Description of what your personality does',
  version: '1.0.0',
  systemPrompt: prompts.system,
  defaultTemperature: 0.7,
  maxTokens: 1024,
  memoryCollections: ['main', 'context'],
  apiEndpoints: ['/api/your-endpoint'],
  uiComponents: ['YourCustomComponent']
}, YourPersonality);

export { default as YourPersonality } from './your-personality-id.personality';
```

### 5. Add Personality to the System Registry

Update the main personalities index file:

```typescript
// src/personalities/index.ts

// Import all personalities
import './able-gpt';
import './renascend-gpt';
import './your-personality-id';

// Re-export the personality service
export * from '../services/personalityService';
```

### 6. Create API Routes

Add API routes for your personality:

```typescript
// src/pages/api/personalities/[personalityId]/[...endpoints].ts

import { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from 'next';
import { loadPersonality } from '../../../../services/personalityService';

export default async function handler(
  req: NextApiRequest,
  res: NextApiResponse
) {
  const { personalityId, endpoints } = req.query;

  if (!personalityId || typeof personalityId !== 'string') {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Missing personality ID' });
  }

  try {
    const personality = await loadPersonality(personalityId);

    // Route handling based on endpoint
    const endpoint = Array.isArray(endpoints) ? endpoints[0] : endpoints;

    switch (endpoint) {
      case 'chat':
        // Handle chat endpoint
        const { message, context } = req.body;
        const preparedPrompt = await personality.preparePrompt(message, context);

        // Call your LLM service here
        const llmResponse = "LLM response would go here";

        const processedResponse = await personality.processResponse(llmResponse);
        return res.status(200).json({ response: processedResponse });

      // Add more endpoints as needed

      default:
        return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Endpoint not found' });
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error handling personality request:`, error);
    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
  }
}
```

### 7. Add UI Integration

Create a React component to use your personality:

```typescript
// src/components/personalities/YourPersonalityComponent.tsx

import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { usePersonality } from '../../ui/hooks/usePersonality';

export function YourPersonalityComponent() {
  const { 
    personality, 
    loading, 
    error 
  } = usePersonality('your-personality-id');

  const [input, setInput] = useState('');
  const [response, setResponse] = useState('');

  async function handleSubmit(e: React.FormEvent) {
    e.preventDefault();

    try {
      const res = await fetch(
        `/api/personalities/${personality?.id}/chat`,
        {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({ message: input })
        }
      );

      const data = await res.json();
      setResponse(data.response);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error sending message:', error);
    }
  }

  if (loading) return <div>Loading personality...</div>;
  if (error) return <div>Error: {error.message}</div>;

  return (
    <div className="personality-container">
      <h2>{personality?.name}</h2>
      <p>{personality?.description}</p>

      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
        <input
          type="text"
          value={input}
          onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)}
          placeholder="Ask a question..."
        />
        <button type="submit">Send</button>
      </form>

      {response && (
        <div className="response">
          <h3>Response:</h3>
          <p>{response}</p>
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 8. Test Your Personality

Run the built-in test suite on your new personality:

```typescript
// src/test/test-your-personality.ts

import { loadPersonality } from '../services/personalityService';
import { testPersonality } from '../test/personality-test-framework';

async function runTests() {
  try {
    const personality = await loadPersonality('your-personality-id');
    const testsPassed = await testPersonality(personality);

    console.log(`Tests passed: ${testsPassed}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Test error:', error);
  }
